---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Enki Shader Editor — Privacy Policy"
  description="Enki Shader Editor collects no personal data: no internet permission, no ads, no analytics. What each permission is used for."
>
  <Nav />
  <main>
    <section class="section privacy-section">
      <div class="container privacy">
        <span class="section-label">Enki Shader Editor</span>
        <h1 class="section-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="section-desc">
          Enki Shader Editor does not collect, store or share any personal
          data. It has no internet permission, so it cannot send anything off
          your device, and it contains no ads, analytics or tracking.
        </p>

        <h2>Permissions</h2>
        <p>
          Each is asked for only when you use the feature, and you can refuse
          or revoke it at any time:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Camera:</strong> shows the camera image as a texture in
            your shaders. Frames stay on the device and are never saved unless
            you capture the output.</li>
          <li><strong>Microphone:</strong> lets shaders react to sound. Audio
            is analysed as it plays and never recorded or saved.</li>
          <li><strong>System audio capture:</strong> the same, for audio
            playing on the device. Android shows a notification while it's
            on.</li>
          <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> progress for long captures and
            audio input.</li>
          <li><strong>Storage</strong> (older Android versions only): saves the
            images, videos and exports you ask for.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Sensors such as the accelerometer, gyroscope and light sensor feed
          your shaders while they run. Their readings are never stored or sent
          anywhere.
        </p>

        <h2>Your files</h2>
        <p>
          Your shaders, textures and settings are kept in the app's private
          storage. Captures and exports go only where you choose to save or
          share them.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions or suggestions: email Dan Wills at
          <a href="mailto:gdanzo@gmail.com">gdanzo@gmail.com</a>, or open an
          issue on
          <a href="https://github.com/danwills/EnkiShaderEditor/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy-section {
    padding-top: 9rem;
  }

  .privacy h2 {
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }

  .privacy p,
  .privacy ul {
    max-width: 40rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .privacy ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .privacy li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
